time=2026-10-26T23:01:09.018Z level=INFO msg="model prompt" record=prov-2026-6b30af71 attempt=1 prompt="## The change\n\nthe recordClasses function reads, from the sedum tool, the class of every record in a tree.\n\n## Constraints on it\n\n- The function receives a pointer to a repo and the tree path string, in that order\n- The function returns a map from string to string and a boolean, in that order\n- The map's keys are record ids and its values are classes\n- The generators directory is the \"generators\" directory inside the tree when it exists\n- The sedum program is the value of the SEDUM_BIN environment variable when it is non-empty\n- When SEDUM_BIN is empty, the program is the command \"sedum\" found on the executable search path\n- The function runs the program with the arguments grow, --check, --generators, the generators directory, --records, the records directory, --output and the tree path, in that order\n- The records directory is the tree path joined with the repo's Config.Dir\n- The arguments include no --only, so every record of the records directory is listed\n- The program runs with the tree as working directory\n- Only standard output is read\n- The function returns a nil map and false when the program could not be started, including when the binary is missing\n- A class line does not start with whitespace\n- A class line's first word consists only of lowercase letters\n- A class line has a second word\n- Words are separated by spaces or tabs\n- For a class line the class is the first word and the record id is the second word\n- When several class lines name the same record id, the first one is kept\n- After the program has run, the function returns the map, possibly empty, and true\n- The repo parameter is a pointer to the repo struct defined in common_run.go of package main, whose Config.Dir field is a string holding the records directory relative to the repo root\n- When the tree has no generators directory, the function uses a newly created empty temporary directory, made with os.MkdirTemp in the default temporary location with the name prefix \"sedum-empty-\"\n- That empty temporary directory is removed before the function returns\n- When that empty temporary directory cannot be created, the function returns a nil map and false\n- The exit status of the program is ignored\n- A line that starts with whitespace is not a class line\n- A line whose first word ends with a colon is not a class line\n- A line whose first word is a number is not a class line\n- The function owns the import of os, as a value import of a standard-library package\n- The function owns the import of os/exec, as a value import of a standard-library package\n- The function owns the import of path/filepath, as a value import of a standard-library package\n- The function owns the import of strings, as a value import of a standard-library package\n\n## Files\n\nThese files exist and are the only ones the actions below may reach:\n\n- cmd/provenance/migration_run.go (package go; injection points: decls, imports)\n\n## Actions\n\n{\n  \"actions\": [\n    {\n      \"action\": \"addImport\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Imports one package.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"path\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The import path.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"imports\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"path\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"setConst\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Defines one package-level constant, replacing an earlier version of it.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"code\": {\n          \"type\": \"literal\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The whole const declaration, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The constant's name.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"decls\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"code\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"setFunction\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Defines one top-level function, replacing an earlier version of it.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"code\": {\n          \"type\": \"literal\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The whole function declaration, signature and body, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The function's name.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"decls\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"code\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"setMethod\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Defines one method, replacing an earlier version of it.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"code\": {\n          \"type\": \"literal\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The whole method declaration, receiver, signature and body, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The method's name.\"\n        },\n        \"receiver\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The receiver's type name, without a pointer star.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"decls\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"code\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"setType\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Defines one named type, replacing an earlier version of it.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"code\": {\n          \"type\": \"literal\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The whole type declaration, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The type's name.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"decls\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"code\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"action\": \"setVar\",\n      \"package\": \"go\",\n      \"description\": \"Defines one package-level variable, replacing an earlier version of it.\",\n      \"kwargs\": {\n        \"code\": {\n          \"type\": \"literal\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The whole var declaration, as gofmt-formatted Go.\"\n        },\n        \"file\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The Go file to write into. It must be one of the authorized files.\"\n        },\n        \"name\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"description\": \"The variable's name.\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"anchor\": [\n        \"decls\"\n      ],\n      \"requires\": [\n        \"code\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n"
time=2026-10-26T23:01:19.490Z level=INFO msg="model responded" record=prov-2026-6b30af71 attempt=1 response="{\"invocations\": [{\"action\": \"addImport\", \"kwargs\": {\"file\": \"cmd/provenance/migration_run.go\", \"path\": \"os\"}}, {\"action\": \"addImport\", \"kwargs\": {\"file\": \"cmd/provenance/migration_run.go\", \"path\": \"os/exec\"}}, {\"action\": \"addImport\", \"kwargs\": {\"file\": \"cmd/provenance/migration_run.go\", \"path\": \"path/filepath\"}}, {\"action\": \"addImport\", \"kwargs\": {\"file\": \"cmd/provenance/migration_run.go\", \"path\": \"strings\"}}, {\"action\": \"setFunction\", \"kwargs\": {\"file\": \"cmd/provenance/migration_run.go\", \"name\": \"recordClasses\", \"code\": \"func recordClasses(r *repo, treePath string) (map[string]string, bool) {\\n\\tbin := os.Getenv(\\\"SEDUM_BIN\\\")\\n\\tif bin == \\\"\\\" {\\n\\t\\tbin = \\\"sedum\\\"\\n\\t}\\n\\tgenerators := filepath.Join(treePath, \\\"generators\\\")\\n\\tif info, err := os.Stat(generators); err != nil || !info.IsDir() {\\n\\t\\tempty, err := os.MkdirTemp(\\\"\\\", \\\"sedum-empty-\\\")\\n\\t\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn nil, false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tdefer os.RemoveAll(empty)\\n\\t\\tgenerators = empty\\n\\t}\\n\\trecords := filepath.Join(treePath, r.Config.Dir)\\n\\tcmd := exec.Command(bin, \\\"grow\\\", \\\"--check\\\", \\\"--generators\\\", generators, \\\"--records\\\", records, \\\"--output\\\", treePath)\\n\\tcmd.Dir = treePath\\n\\tout, err := cmd.Output()\\n\\tif err != nil {\\n\\t\\tif _, ok := err.(*exec.ExitError); !ok {\\n\\t\\t\\treturn nil, false\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\tclasses := make(map[string]string)\\n\\tfor _, line := range strings.Split(string(out), \\\"\\\\n\\\") {\\n\\t\\tif line == \\\"\\\" || line[0] == ' ' || line[0] == '\\\\t' {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tfields := strings.FieldsFunc(line, func(c rune) bool { return c == ' ' || c == '\\\\t' })\\n\\t\\tif len(fields) < 2 {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tclass := fields[0]\\n\\t\\tlower := class != \\\"\\\"\\n\\t\\tfor _, c := range class {\\n\\t\\t\\tif c < 'a' || c > 'z' {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tlower = false\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tbreak\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tif !lower {\\n\\t\\t\\tcontinue\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\tid := fields[1]\\n\\t\\tif _, seen := classes[id]; !seen {\\n\\t\\t\\tclasses[id] = class\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\treturn classes, true\\n}\"}}]}" prompt_tokens=3049 completion_tokens=2862
